<title>INDIA: Rising arrivals ground Indian soybean prices.</title>
<headline>Rising arrivals ground Indian soybean prices.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean prices on Thursday fell by 100 rupees per tonne on increased arrivals against limited demand in central Indian markets, dealers said.</p>
<p>Business volume was dull and the undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were up by 100 rupees per tonne on limited supply from plants and refineries on dull volumes but firm undertone.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were almost steady on weak tone. Soymeal yellow was $280-285 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) west coast Indian ports for export. The undertone was easy. Rapeseed extraction was $105-106 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) in bulk for export and was 3,600-3,650 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on Rail) condition.</p>
